The root cause of the bug appears to be related to the improper handling of the `stageName` when multiple batches are processed during the package installation, which could lead to incorrect stage naming and subsequent exceptions in resource creation or upgrades. Additionally, the failure to handle scenarios where components are missing from the new stack led to system exceptions that interrupted the process instead of allowing for graceful recovery.

