```java
stageName = String.format(INSTALL_PACKAGES_FULL_NAME + ". Batch %d of %d", batchId, batchCount);
```
```java
throw new IllegalArgumentException(String.format("Repo version %s is not available for stack %s", desiredRepoVersion, stackId));
```
```java
throw new SystemException(String.format("Exception while accessing component %s of service %s for stack %s", component.getServiceName(), component.getServiceComponentName(), stackId));
```
Reason:
The bug occurs due to improper naming of the `stageName` when handling multiple batches, which can result in exceptions during resource creation. Additionally, the absence of components in the new stack is not adequately managed, leading to system exceptions when attempting to access non-existent components.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
stageName = INSTALL_PACKAGES_FULL_NAME;
```
```java
LOG.warn(String.format("Exception while accessing component %s of service %s for stack %s", component.getServiceComponentName(), component.getServiceName(), stackId));
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the `stageName` is correctly set for the case when there is only one batch, preventing incorrect naming and subsequent failures. Moreover, the warning log is introduced to handle cases where components are missing from the new stack gracefully, allowing the process to continue without throwing a system exception.


